mina: I started following them and saw them go into a cafe
mina: Ruby was...beautiful. She had long, flowing hair, soft features and delicate hands
mina: She laughed and gently touched Josephine's hand and I felt my blood boil
mina: How dare she touch her and make her smile like that. Josephine is MINE!

mina: I followed them to the park, They walked hand in hand. She looked at him like she was the sun
mina: And I realized... She never looked at me like that
mina: All those years protecting, loving yet she looked at a stranger as if she was everything
mina: Why?...
mina: Why was'nt I enough

mina: I went home that night and cried until there were no ears left
mina: Then I slowly became angry 

n: She is mine
n: She has always been mine
n: I protected her, loved her and sacrificed everything for her yet she chose someone else

mina: I looked at the ring I had bought to give her and finally propose to make her mine
mina: But she was never mine. IN fact she was never going to be mine
mina: Because I was too afraid to tell her how I felt and now....
mina: It was too late

mina: I could'nt take it anymore. I had to see her myself, I had to know
mina: So I had asked Josephine if I could meet her and suprisingly she agreed, so I prepared myself and went to the local cafe
mina: And there she was....

n: You must be Ruby?

ruby: Ah, You must be Mina. Jose talks about you all the time, You're his childhood friend right?

n: I'm more than a friend I've know him for 15 years and I've protected and loved him

ruby: Oh I know. He or should I say she tells me everything
ruby: How you follow her around, how you scare away anyone who tried to get close to her and even how you treat her as a possesion

n: That's not true

ruby: Isn't it? She told me she felt trapped, She told me you smothered her and she needed space
ruby: And I gave her the space she needed. I let her breath, I let her be herself

mina: His words stabbed me like knifes

ruby: You want to know why she chose me. Beacause I accepted her for who she was and did not try to change her nor claim her
ruby: I just loved her

mina: She smied. A soft, innocent smile and I wanted to kill her
mina: But I could not do it at least not right now
mina: I went home and thought about it for weeks, every scenario and possibility out there
mina: If I killed him, Josephine would be free and most importantly she would be mine

mina: But she would be sad, she would grieve and she would eentually hate me
mina: Unless...
mina: I killed her too, unless I set her free from this world, unless I made sure that if she was not with me she would be with no one else
mina: It was twisted but to me that was the only way

mina: Ruby could never be with her, she could only be with me, she could only be mine
mina: So I drafted a plan, bought a knife and followed them to their date
mina: And I waited......

mina: They had gone to a park
mina: The park was empty, moon full and they were sitting on a bench, holding hands and kissing
mina: I crept closer and the closer I got the more my heart pounded, but my hands were locked in to the knife, it was too late to stop now

mina: I could hear Josephine's laugh. That beautiful laugh, the laugh I would never hear again
mina: And then....
mina: I had struck

mina: Ruby fell first. He did not scream, his body simply collapsed
mina: I looked down at him and could see his blood pooling from underneath his body
mina: Josephine simply stared, her eyes were wide, horrified

jose: Mina?....
jose: What....WHat did you do?....

n: I am setting you free, I am saving you

mina: She tried to run but she was not as fast as me. I grabbed her and held her close
mina: I told her I loved her
mina: And then...
mina: I plunged the knife into her heart

jose: ...Why?

mina: She whispered those words and then she was gone
mina: I sat there holding her body, crying, sobbing...
mina: Wishing I had said something sooner, Wishing I had confessed
mina: But it was too late, It was always too late....

detective: And that is what happened?
detective: You killed them both because of your love for Josephine?

mina: ....Yes

detective: Mina...
detective: Love isn't about obsession or control
detective: Love is about letting go
detective: If you truly loved her...You would have let her be happy

mina: You are right, You are soo right but it does not matter anymore
mina: She is gone, and I am alone the way I always feared
jump ending/